items.body:
Allow inline forms to submit a follow-up message with two layers:

1. **Display layer:** A concise, user-friendly message shown in chat.
2. **Agent layer:** Exact instructions and structured arguments delivered to the agent.

Example proposed API:
```
window.openai.sendFollowUpMessage({
  displayText: "Extract Markdown from the submitted URL",
  prompt: "Execute tool-<xyz>.",
  arguments: {
    arg1: "arg1 value,
    arg2: "arg2 value"
  }
});
```

Show the display text by default, with an expandable “View submitted details” section containing the full agent payload.
This would let validated forms initiate precise tool requests without cluttering chat with execution instructions or requiring a custom MCP bridge. Existing permission and approval rules should continue to apply.
